[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: AI integration
OPTIONS:
  VIEW_STYLE: Table

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @requirement

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Requirements for the AI integration feature. UIDs: REQ-BE-080 .. 089. Requirements in the mobile and dashboard apps that build on it get a ``Parent`` relation to a requirement here.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BE-080
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: AI buddy
STATEMENT: >>>
The backend shall offer an AI assistant, the 'AI buddy', that a logged-in user can chat with through the API. The AI buddy answers questions about agenda items and tasks and carries out instructions on them by calling tools (REQ-BE-085), using a Google Gemini model.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Family members can plan in plain language ('put football training for FC Club JO15-1 on Tuesdays at 18:00') instead of filling in forms.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BE-081
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: AI settings in the web admin
STATEMENT: >>>
An administrator shall be able to switch the AI buddy on and off, and set the Gemini API key, the model, the system prompt and the number of earlier messages sent as context (REQ-BE-087) on an 'AI buddy' settings page in the web admin. The AI buddy is off until an administrator switches it on; switching it off keeps all other settings. The model is chosen from the models available to the API key, as listed by the Gemini API. After saving, the API key is never shown again in full (only its last four characters). The page shall state that chat messages, and the agenda and task data the AI buddy reads, are sent to Google.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-BE-080

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BE-082
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Default system prompt
STATEMENT: >>>
The backend shall ship a default system prompt in Dutch, which is used until an administrator changes it. The administrator can edit it and restore the default. Independent of the editable prompt, the backend shall give the model the current date, time and weekday (Europe/Amsterdam), the name of the calling user, and the names of the people in the planner, so that editing the prompt cannot remove that context.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-BE-081

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BE-098
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Thinking level
STATEMENT: >>>
On the settings page (REQ-BE-081), right after the model, an administrator shall be able to set a thinking level (standard, low, medium, high or extra high) for the AI buddy. Standard means the model's own default. The backend shall only send the chosen level to Gemini 3 and 4 models; other models ignore the setting.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Sending a thinking level to a model older than Gemini 3 is rejected by the Gemini API as an error, so it is limited to the model generations that support it.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-BE-081

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BE-083
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Unavailable until configured
STATEMENT: >>>
While the AI buddy is switched off (REQ-BE-081), or no API key or no model is set, the AI buddy shall be unavailable: the API reports it as not configured, and chat requests get a Dutch error message. A Gemini call that fails with a connection error, a timeout (no answer within 60 seconds) or an HTTP 5xx status shall be tried again up to two more times, after 1 and after 2 seconds; HTTP 4xx errors are not retried. When the last attempt fails, the request shall get a Dutch error message and the user's message is kept. Each attempt is recorded as a separate call (REQ-BE-091).
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-BE-080

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BE-084
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Same rights as the calling user
STATEMENT: >>>
Every tool call shall run with the rights of the user who sent the message, with the same checks as the REST API: the AI buddy can read what that user can read, create, change and delete agenda items only for people the user manages (REQ-BE-021), create, change and delete tasks only for people the user manages (REQ-BE-022), and cannot change imported agenda items (REQ-BE-043). A refused tool call returns the Dutch error message to the model, so that it can explain it to the user.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-BE-080
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-BE-021
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-BE-022

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BE-085
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Agenda and task tools
STATEMENT: >>>
The AI buddy shall have tools to search, read, create, change and delete agenda items and tasks. Searching filters on a date range (at most 180 days, like the mobile API), person and text in the title. Creating and changing support the same fields as the REST API, including start and end time and repeat options.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-BE-080

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BE-086
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Confirm before deleting
STATEMENT: >>>
The AI buddy shall delete an agenda item or task only after the user confirmed that specific deletion in the chat. The delete tool first returns what would be deleted; the deletion only happens when the model calls it again with that confirmation after the user's reply.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A misunderstood instruction must not silently remove someone's planning.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-BE-085

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BE-087
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Conversation per user
STATEMENT: >>>
The backend shall keep one conversation per user, so that it can be shown again on any of the user's devices and the AI buddy has the earlier messages as context: the last N messages including the new one, where N is set by an administrator (REQ-BE-081) between 2 and 100, default 20. The user can clear their conversation. Other users, administrators included, cannot read it through the app or the web admin, except in the AI call log while an administrator has turned the debug log on (REQ-BE-092).
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-BE-080

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BE-088
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Bounded tool use
STATEMENT: >>>
For one user message the backend shall make at most 10 tool calls; after that it asks the model for a final answer without tools.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Protects against loops that keep calling tools and run up API costs.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-BE-080

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BE-089
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Changes are normal changes
STATEMENT: >>>
Agenda items and tasks created, changed or deleted by the AI buddy shall be stored like changes through the REST API, so they show up on the wall tablet (REQ-BE-001) and in the apps without further action.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-BE-080
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-BE-001
